  "step_3": "The decision reason is about skewness and prefers the more left-skewed lottery. However, in this case, both lotteries are right-skewed (more probability on the zero outcome), and no lottery is left-skewed. Therefore, the decision reason is not applicable to the decision problem. Furthermore, the individual's justification is based on comparing the probability of loss and the size of the loss, not on skewness. There is no reference to favorable vs unfavorable outcome probabilities in terms of distribution shape. Since the reason cannot be applied (due to the nature of the lotteries) and the individual did not use the concept of skewness in their reasoning, the decision reason was not used. The individual used a different reasoning principle (likely minimizing expected loss or risk). Thus, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
